# Offline sync

`lib/sync/queue.ts` is the only write path from the field app.

- Every queued write carries a `client_event_id` (uuid v4, generated on device).
- Server-side idempotency comes from a unique constraint on `client_event_id`.
  A duplicate insert is caught and treated as SUCCESS, not an error.
- Flush on reconnect, on app focus, and on a timer.
- Ordering is preserved per assignment.
- A 4xx does not retry forever. Surface it.
- The queue must survive a browser restart and a mid-flush kill.

If a task seems to need a second sync implementation, stop and re-read the codebase. It does not.

## Exception: live position (UI-7, owner 2026-10-04)

- `report_position` and `stop_sharing_position` are called from `lib/field/position-share.ts` only, NOT through the queue.
- A position is ephemeral. Replaying an old one later would be wrong, so it is never queued, never written to Dexie or any storage, and is simply dropped when offline or on error.
- This is the only field write outside `lib/sync/queue.ts`. Do not add a second one.
